{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1217104-talassi-beasts","id":1217104,"title":"Talassi beasts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-09T13:57:00-07:00","id":1217104,"title":"Talassi beasts","content":"What exactly differentiates them from anakim? What about their horrors, sound pretty similar to Ingumas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T14:14:32-07:00","id":1217115,"title":"","content":"Talassii are the nightmares of confinement as opposed to the Anakim who are the nightmares of hopelessness. There is potential for overlap there, but they aren't strictly the same. One can be confined, but still have hope and one can be hopeless whilst unconfined. Anakim are the unstoppable forces, the thing that your only hope for surviving is that it doesn't come near you or decides it doesn't wish to kill you. Talassii, you're chained up in a basement, you're in jail, you're in a system of tunnels that are pressing on you.<br /> <br /> Now as for the Inguma, well the Inguma are the fear of the outsider or others. You know your neighbors and your friends they aren't chaining you up in a basement for their insane purposes, that new guy on the block though, you haven't met them yet. They keep to themselves, you don't know anything about them. They might very well chain you up in their basement for whatever insane reasons they have and who knows what they'll do to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T14:22:10-07:00","id":1217119,"title":"","content":"In the simplest terms: One is a giant the other is a spider. The giant is coming through that wall. The spider is laying a trap outside the door for you to step in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T14:54:38-07:00","id":1217136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1217104-talassi-beasts?p=1217119#post1217119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the simplest terms: One is a giant the other is a spider. The giant is coming through that wall. The spider is laying a trap outside the door for you to step in.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Alternatively, the Anakim is the judge and jury who decides your fate, while the Talassi is the warden in charge of the prison complex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T14:58:15-07:00","id":1217141,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys. Now about the horror itself? It's described as also capable of being pretty human like","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T15:02:31-07:00","id":1217144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1217104-talassi-beasts?p=1217141#post1217141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks guys. Now about the horror itself? It's described as also capable of being pretty human like</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Makes sense, as from what I understand, they were born to be jailors. You could have a Talassi who takes the form of a kidnapper, grabbing people off the street and locking them away inside their custom designed labyrinths. You get across the fear of confinement, without them having to be some kind of spooky monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T15:13:02-07:00","id":1217148,"title":"","content":"So what would separate them from inguna horrors when talassi ones are more humanoid? Does the book go in depth about their ancient anathema","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T15:28:52-07:00","id":1217154,"title":"","content":"If I remember right Talassi can be more then just humanoid, there basically any monster that imprison and confine someone. I think I remember being a princess kidnapping dragon as an option","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T15:34:45-07:00","id":1217159,"title":"","content":"To be more specific (still appreciate the answer though) what would be key differences between humanoid talassi and inguna horrors","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T15:41:39-07:00","id":1217163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1217104-talassi-beasts?p=1217148#post1217148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what would separate them from inguna horrors when talassi ones are more humanoid? Does the book go in depth about their ancient anathema</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Inguma represent the fear of the outsider, that alien thing that does not belong with the rest of the group.<br /> <br /> They are the embodiment of xenophobia, which actually leaves the game wide open for all forms of bigotry and intolerance. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-09-2018, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T16:02:53-07:00","id":1217173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1217104-talassi-beasts?p=1217136#post1217136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Alternatively, the Anakim is the judge and jury who decides your fate, while the Talassi is the warden in charge of the prison complex.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Irony: this is exactly what's happening in my current game for an NPC trio. The third is the sheriff who is an Ugallu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T16:12:51-07:00","id":1217175,"title":"","content":"Not to mention Inugami are just other or alien, they can look like some fear based on racial or ethnic threat. They can look like a humanoid thing like the rake, slender man, or some uncanny valley monster. Then finally they could just be freaking eldritch horrors straight out of lovecraftian mythos. They aren't restricted like that. <br /> <br /> Taalassii are just confinement, I think one of the later examples in the player's guide of a nightmare being created mentions the Talassii beast's Horror is called the chain shark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T16:43:48-07:00","id":1217186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1217104-talassi-beasts?p=1217175#post1217175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the chain shark.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why does that sound like a professional wrestling move!?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T02:39:40-07:00","id":1217307,"title":"","content":"From the top of my head:<br /> Some possible Talassii horrors would be a spider, a dragon, a faery king or queen, a witch, a cyclops, a troll, an uncanny valley corrupt corporate executive... anything that 'chains you down' in some shape or form.<br /> As long as imprisonment is a theme, it's fair game.<br /> Just like a dragon can be Anakim, Eshmaki, Ugallu, Makara, or Namtaru, depending on your focus, themes are more important than just appearance.<br /> <br /> <br /> So the key difference between humanoid Inguma and Talassii would be the Inguma looking off in some way, strange, alien. Wrong shade or colour of skin (pale white, blue, green, translucent, iridescent...), unnatural eyes (Atavistic, red iris, black scelera, cross-shaped pupils, Sharingan, whathaveyou), unnatural hair (think Zerg-Kerrigan for example), limbs or other features that are somehow off (too long arms, lack of facial features) jumbled limbs (switch legs and arms for example) and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BtcP3gCGDyQ\" target=\"_blank\">corresponding movements that are just wrong</a>.<br /> <br /> The Talassii is less clear-cut, but something about him has to carry the idea of confinement: a tree-person, a spider-hybrid, maybe a king with a broken crown, or some other sort of authority. I imagine prison wards, asylum docs and the like to show up quite a bit.<br /> Plant-life can give you ideas: Venus-fly trap and other carnivorous plants seem practically MADE for the Talassii Horror.<br /> You could have very strong people, e.g. bodybuilders and wrestlers, whose ability to keep you in their grip is strengthened: extremely large hands, spiked hands, multiple hands...<br /> On the opposite, 'children' might qualify, too, especially if the horror is some sort of baby that 'chains you down' by having you unable to leave it alone - or live with the guilty conscience abandoning a baby brings with it. Make it look extra sickly, then add some other horror template (Witcher's botchling, anyone?)<br /> <br /> You could go the Anakim's 'force of nature' route and have a 'unsatisfying dead-end job' as a Horror as well, I guess.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T03:21:53-07:00","id":1217317,"title":"","content":"One other suggestion for Talassii (I kinda need to get the Player's handbook so just going from the Descriptions here) Perhaps &quot;Mary&quot; from Silent Hill 2 could be one... She in Life represented not being able to move on, being unable to let go and having to stay with her. She was Bed Ridden, unable to care for herself. Then comes the End of SH2... and she becomes..<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"http://silenthill.wikia.com/wiki/Mary_(boss\" target=\"_blank\">http://silenthill.wikia.com/wiki/Mary_(boss</a>)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> A Nightmarish creature that floats around and attacks with it's Tongue....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T04:40:28-07:00","id":1217332,"title":"","content":"Don't forget, that because of their nature, Talassii horrors are often mistaken with other families (and they are OK with it). So that brief &quot;requirement&quot; for a Beast's Horror to look like something is even briefer in this case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T05:22:50-07:00","id":1217339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1217104-talassi-beasts?p=1217307#post1217307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">anything that 'chains you down' in some shape or form.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VsiKOJOXMJU\" data-code=\"VsiKOJOXMJU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/VsiKOJOXMJU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T12:33:03-07:00","id":1217473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1217104-talassi-beasts?p=1217307#post1217307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">anything that 'chains you down' in some shape or form.</div> </div> </div> </div>This thread might start devolving.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qXZM5bxoccc\" data-code=\"qXZM5bxoccc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/qXZM5bxoccc/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T15:47:24-07:00","id":1217511,"title":"","content":"So basically, humanoid talassi represent jailers, supervisors, or even a monstrous teacher that looks over students in detention, and be symbolic, like the jailer may have chains attached and the teacher may appear right next to you if it seems you even attempt to do something. Meanwhile the inguna are uncanny valley. Odd movements, exaggerated features, maybe even blades coming out of the elbows, but they can even represent a person that comes from nowhere and is instantly popular, yet something seems insidious, like they just know everything and everyone adores them for no clear reason<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> (from the link you put up) don't known how he learnt to do that, but very impressive","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T16:17:57-07:00","id":1217521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1217104-talassi-beasts?p=1217511#post1217511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile the inguna are uncanny valley. Odd movements, exaggerated features, maybe even blades coming out of the elbows, but they can even represent a person that comes from nowhere and is instantly popular, yet something seems insidious, like they just know everything and everyone adores them for no clear reason<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Quite the opposite, in fact. As I said earlier, the Inguma represent <b>Xenophobia.</b><br /> <br /> They are not welcome here, they do not blend in with the rest of the group.<br /> <br /> They do not conform with our system, they are different from us.<br /> <br /> They are a symbol of change, in a society that has long since embraced stagnation.<br /> <br /> They are an aberration from the norm, so they must be shunned.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> And for anybody who thinks that this doesn't fit well as a primordial fear (I've seen at least one person say as much), I strongly disagree.<br /> <br /> Humanity has <b>always feared</b> that which it doesn't understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-10-2018, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T17:18:35-07:00","id":1217532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1217104-talassi-beasts?p=1217154#post1217154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember right Talassi can be more then just humanoid, there basically any monster that imprison and confine someone. I think I remember being a princess kidnapping dragon as an option</div> </div> </div> </div>So like the fae of old that kidnapped children to be servents","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T18:39:11-07:00","id":1217551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1217104-talassi-beasts?p=1217521#post1217521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Quite the opposite, in fact. As I said earlier, the Inguma represent <b>Xenophobia.</b><br /> <br /> They are not welcome here, they do not blend in with the rest of the group.<br /> <br /> They do not conform with our system, they are different from us.<br /> <br /> They are a symbol of change, in a society that has long since embraced stagnation.<br /> <br /> They are an aberration from the norm, so they must be shunned.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> And for anybody who thinks that this doesn't fit well as a primordial fear (I've seen at least one person say as much), I strongly disagree.<br /> <br /> Humanity has <b>always feared</b> that which it doesn't understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fourth line there, doesn't that fit with what I said about some popular person coming from out of nowhere? It's actually an example in the players guide","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T18:55:11-07:00","id":1217554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1217104-talassi-beasts?p=1217551#post1217551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fourth line there, doesn't that fit with what I said about some popular person coming from out of nowhere? It's actually an example in the players guide</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It kind of does. But most people have an instinctive fear of sudden changes being forcefully inserted into their lives. As the saying goes, some people have to hit rock bottom before they finally decide to change their ways.<br /> <br /> Random mystery person showing up on the scene and acting like they own the place is bound to upset the status quo. Depending on which group they become popular with, somebody at the top or bottom of the chain is going to view them as a threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-10-2018, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T06:14:03-07:00","id":1217643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1217104-talassi-beasts?p=1217521#post1217521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Quite the opposite, in fact. As I said earlier, the Inguma represent <b>Xenophobia.</b><br /> <br /> They are not welcome here, they do not blend in with the rest of the group.<br /> <br /> They do not conform with our system, they are different from us.<br /> <br /> They are a symbol of change, in a society that has long since embraced stagnation.<br /> <br /> They are an aberration from the norm, so they must be shunned.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> And for anybody who thinks that this doesn't fit well as a primordial fear (I've seen at least one person say as much), I strongly disagree.<br /> <br /> Humanity has <b>always feared</b> that which it doesn't understand.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have to disagree to a degree here, they can represent the fear of a group, a literal outsider, but they can also represent the fear of an individual as well. (fear of the other)<br /> So there is that person that everyone is OK with, acts nice and all with them, but YOU know he is different.<br /> <br /> Edit: Well, disagree may not be the correct word here, I mean you only present one side of the Inguma, I say there is an other one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24132,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","user":"IceBen","date":". 05-11-2018, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T20:24:28-07:00","id":1220411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1217104-talassi-beasts?p=1217643#post1217643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have to disagree to a degree here, they can represent the fear of a group, a literal outsider, but they can also represent the fear of an individual as well. (fear of the other)<br /> So there is that person that everyone is OK with, acts nice and all with them, but YOU know he is different.<br /> <br /> Edit: Well, disagree may not be the correct word here, I mean you only present one side of the Inguma, I say there is an other one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I understand what you're getting at with Inguma representing a group, in which their victim plays the role of the outsider, which can be equally as frightening.<br /> <br /> I'm just having trouble imagining how you'd portray them as a collective without a liberal abundance of Horrorspawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa